WEBVTT

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.050
<i>The eighth game is about to begin!</i>

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.220
SAYAKA KATAHARA
THE DAUGHTER OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.310
Please welcome our first fighter!

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.600
<i>He is the roughest of wrestlers,</i>

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.770
<i>whose older brothers are yokozuna,</i>
<i>grand champion sumo wrestlers.</i>

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.270
<i>He's not just satisfied with fighting</i>
<i>inside the sumo ring.</i>

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.070
<i>He’ll take on any assault or threat</i>
<i>if his clients ask him to.</i>

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.660
<i>His bad attitude is at its peak.</i>

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.080
<i>The troublemaker takes to the field</i>
<i>carrying the honor of the sumo world.</i>

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.250
<i>Standing at 194 cm.</i>
<i>and weighing 159 kg.,</i>

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.790
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>seven wins and no losses.</i>

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.920
His assets total
22 billion 116 million 100 thousand yen.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>Representing MAGATANIEN, also known as</i>
<i>the Brawler of the Sumo Ring,</i>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.890
<i>Takeru Kiohzan!</i>

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.150
TAKERU KIOHZAN
REPRESENTATIVE FIGHTER OF MAGATANIEN

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.230
<i>How irreverent!</i>

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.940
<i>That's the special loincloth</i>
<i>only yokozuna are allowed to wear.</i>

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.380
JUZO MAGATANI, PRESIDENT
SAKURA AKIYAMA, SECRETARY

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.380
GEN SHIKANO
CHAIRMAN OF GANDAI

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>Yoisho!</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>Yoisho!</i>

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.160
HARUO KOHNO, REP. FIGHTER OF NENTENDO
(ELIMINATED IN THE FIRST ROUND)

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.290
Oops. Sorry, bro.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.540
Are you hurt?

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.750
<i>He pulled me up?</i>

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.090
<i>No way! I weigh more than 300 kg.!</i>

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.920
Hey, are you leaving so soon?

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.760
The next game is going to be fun.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.970
Watch it before you leave.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.100
Who the heck are you?

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.560
You don't need to know my name.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.310
I'm just a pro-wrestler passing by.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.900
It's pro-wrestling versus sumo wrestling.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.690
They're often compared to each other,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.650
but it's time to decide who is stronger!

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.200
Here the next man comes!

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:46.540
<i>This angel of destruction came from hell</i>
<i>to represent the pro-wrestlers.</i>

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:52.130
<i>He's entering second with confidence,</i>
<i>as if to say his opponent is inferior.</i>

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.710
<i>Standing at 196 cm. and weighing 141 kg.,</i>

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.260
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>57 wins and one loss.</i>

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:07.390
His total assets are
555 billion 111 million 250 thousand yen.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.730
Representing GANDAI,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:15.730
<i>also known as Hell's Angel,</i>
<i>Jun Sekibayashi!</i>

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.950
JUN SEKIBAYASHI
FIGHTER OF GANDAI

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.660
<i>-</i>What?!
<i>-This bastard!</i>

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:26.910
OHMA TOKITA, REP. FIGHTER

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.200
KAEDE AKIYAMA
K. YAMASHITA

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.290
His hairstyle is...

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.790
<i>Sekibayashi's hairstyle is</i>
<i>the official one for sumo wrestlers!</i>

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.300
No, wait, it's back to front,
breaking the rule among sumo wrestlers.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:42.800
<i>It means pro-wrestling presents</i>
<i>a huge challenge to sumo wrestling.</i>

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.720
<i>Piece of crap!</i>

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.930
<i>I'll blow you away.</i>

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.900
"CONVICTIONS"

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.870
You're mad, aren't you?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.040
If you lose your temper so easily,
you lack a sense of professionalism.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:43.170
Don't forget that we're entertainers
before fighters.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:45.670
Okay.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.880
You two, take your positions.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.310
-You piss me off.
-<i>Such power!</i>

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.900
Too easy.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.150
Hey, Sekibayashi!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.400
Don't get carried away, trickster.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.990
<i>Whoa, it's unbelievable!</i>

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.950
<i>Before the referee's command,</i>

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.950
-<i>Kiohzan started attacking!</i>
-<i>Seriously?</i>

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:13.080
<i>Ohma had a very hard time</i>
<i>beating Sekibayashi.</i>

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.410
<i>Though it was a surprise attack,</i>
<i>he was taken down with only one attack?</i>

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.670
Can you go on, Sekibayashi? Come on!

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.830
Pathetic.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:23.840
You bastard!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.920
This is going to hurt a bit, brat.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.430
Remember, kid.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.600
Pro-wrestlers are good actors.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.600
Now that's pro-wrestling! Awesome!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.480
Kiohzan?

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.450
You've got the wrong idea.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.780
Remember, old man.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:56.660
Sumo wrestlers are sturdier
than pro-wrestlers.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.080
That's the spirit.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:04.210
You could be a good pro-wrestler.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.460
<i>Known as Hell's Angel,</i>
<i>Jun Sekibayashi is...</i>

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:10.260
<i>the top fighter of</i>
<i>the Super Japan Pro-Wrestling.</i>

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.970
<i>He's a big name both in the public</i>
<i>and the underground field.</i>

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.430
<i>Receiving all the attacks</i>
<i>from enemies with pride,</i>

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.610
<i>he always smashes them</i>
<i>into smithereens like a heavy tank.</i>

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:31.200
<i>But now, he is being overwhelmed.</i>

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.330
Brat!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.960
Don't get cocky!

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:44.830
<i>He doesn't budge.</i>

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.930
<i>Jerks like you build up their body</i>
<i>just to perform an entertainment show.</i>

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.300
<i>We're not the same.</i>

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.850
<i>As a sumo wrestler, I've built up my body</i>
<i>purely to be strong.</i>

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.350
<i>A person like me can't get beaten</i>
<i>by a trickster like you.</i>

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.690
<i>Oh, it seems Sekibayashi has lost</i>
<i>consciousness!</i>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:15.990
<i>He jumped!</i>

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:20.000
<i>Pro-wrestling isn't just about</i>
<i>punching and kicking.</i>

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.000
<i>Pro-wrestling is about</i>

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.000
<i>fighting in three-dimensional space!</i>

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.920
This kind of fight must be new to you

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.380
as sumo is all about fighting
on a flat field.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.720
I'm not hurt at all, you trash.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.190
That's what I expected to hear.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.660
<i>In a face-off between sumo wrestling and</i>
<i>pro-wrestling, neither is stepping back.</i>

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.370
Hit after hit!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.620
JERRY TYSON, REP. FIGHTER OF 22ND CENTURY
FAX

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.750
Sekibayashi is hitting
backhand chops nonstop!

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.590
So impressive!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.050
Sekibayashi is fighting back!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.840
Go Sekibayashi!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:17.090
Sekibayashi!

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.350
It's amazing.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:28.650
Don't get carried away, old fart!

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.620
<i>Neither of them is backing off at all!</i>

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.200
COSMO IMAI, REP. FIGHTER

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.410
AKIRA NISHIHONJI,
PRESIDENT

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.660
<i>Watch and learn, Cos.</i>

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.960
<i>Sekibayashi has something</i>
<i>you don't have as a fighter.</i>

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.960
<i>Sense it from this game.</i>

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:53.210
<i>If you can find it, you'll be stronger.</i>

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.550
<i>This big shit!</i>

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:59.680
<i>Why doesn't he guard himself?</i>

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.640
<i>Kiohzan keeps carrying out</i>
<i>his violent thrusts!</i>

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.190
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:15.240
<i>He hung on to the end!</i>
<i>This is Jun Sekibayashi!</i>

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.860
<i>He has absorbed all the storm-like attacks</i>
<i>from Kiohzan without guarding!</i>

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.490
Hey, kid.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.120
Has your stamina run out?

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.580
Don't underestimate me, you bastard!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.130
Why don't you block my attacks?
Are you trying to insult me?

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.380
Oh, no! Don't take it the wrong way.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.550
This is my style of pro-wrestling.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:44.310
Shit!

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:48.980
<i>I can't push him back.</i>

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:53.020
Come on. Don't you understand?

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.530
It's my turn, right?

00:10:56.070 --> 00:11:00.280
I'll show you the quintessence
of a pro-wrestler.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.540
Now I'm totally pissed off.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.880
I didn't think I'd have to show
my style of sumo

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.880
to a trickster like you, jerk.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:25.720
<i>What a tragedy for Sekibayashi!</i>

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.230
<i>He was only one step away from the victory</i>
<i>before being regrettably knocked down!</i>

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.940
<i>What happened between them?</i>

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:41.860
<i>What a tragedy for Sekibayashi!</i>

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.200
<i>He was only one step away from the victory</i>
<i>before being regrettably knocked down!</i>

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:49.790
<i>We never thought Kiohzan would use</i>
<i>a technique like that.</i>

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.000
Is that okay?

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.630
The sumo wrestler used a kick!

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.090
<i>Since I was a kid, I've been wondering,</i>

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:02.260
<i>why is sumo so incomplete?</i>

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.760
<i>With a well-trained body,</i>

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.760
<i>why are we only permitted to use</i>
<i>some limited techniques?</i>

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.020
<i>However, at some point,</i>
<i>I finally realized...</i>

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.940
<i>that I can just use a kick.</i>

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:21.950
<i>Damn it!</i>
<i>I lost consciousness for a moment.</i>

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:25.700
Don't fall asleep yet.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:30.120
I'm going to teach you
what true sumo wrestling is.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.580
<i>Wow, a stream of blows!</i>

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.500
<i>The sumo wrestler punches</i>
<i>the pro-wrestler over and over.</i>

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.840
ADAM DUDLEY, REP. FIGHTER OF BOSS BURGER

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.130
Can you really say it's sumo?
That's more like MMA!

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.470
Yes, it's sumo.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:43.590
Excuse me?

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:49.010
Sumo was originally a mixed martial art
in ancient times like <i>pankration</i>.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.640
<i>Once in an ancient time,</i>
<i>there was a match.</i>

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:58.560
<i>It was the first </i>kakuryoku<i> match</i>
<i>written in Japan's oldest history book.</i>

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:01.570
<i>What decided the game was kicking.</i>

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.240
SUMO WRESTLING

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:07.410
<i>Before the present sumo was created,</i>
<i>it was called </i>kakuryoku<i>.</i>

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:08.370
KAKURYOKU

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:13.410
<i>It was a martial art with no limits of</i>
<i>blowing, throwing, grappling, or choking.</i>

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:17.170
Undoubtedly, that's sumo, or rather...

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.460
I'd call it ancient sumo.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:25.090
You're quite a guy, old man.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.340
How long can you continue
without guarding?

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.100
You must want to die, huh?

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.140
I don't care, though.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:35.480
If you want to die,
I'd be happy to kill you!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.230
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:41.980
<i>This little attack cannot beat me.</i>

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:43.990
He's smiling.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.990
How is he able to smile?

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.200
The odds are completely against him.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.120
Is he insane?

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.170
<i>My knee may be damaged.</i>

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.300
<i>But so what?</i>

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:08.180
<i>I don't care if bones are broken</i>
<i>or flesh is torn.</i>

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:15.140
<i>Sumo boy, you look like</i>
<i>you're running out of breath.</i>

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.930
<i>But that's natural.</i>

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:21.900
<i>Sumo wrestlers have bodies</i>
<i>dedicated to fighting for a short time.</i>

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.900
<i>Your style of sumo must interact</i>
<i>quite badly</i>

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.900
<i>with the authentic sumo wrestler's body.</i>

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.030
<i>What's your next plan?</i>
<i>Shaping up your body?</i>

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:34.040
<i>Going on a diet or stamina training?</i>

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:37.660
<i>Is that really "sumo"?</i>

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:39.750
What a load of rubbish!

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.460
Son of a bitch!

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:49.630
<i>Kid, you really remind me of myself</i>

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.640
<i>before I became a true pro-wrestler.</i>

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.180
Fall on the ground right now!

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:55.850
Shitty old man!

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.930
<i>Head lock!</i>

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.770
<i>You're who I was at that time.</i>

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.360
<i>Guard yourself, please!</i>

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:09.530
<i>It was when I was slightly over 30.</i>

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.370
<i>I was in the corner for Kurachi,</i>

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.450
<i>who joined a game of Vale Tudo,</i>
<i>where anything goes.</i>

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.250
KARUGO KURACHI
SUPER JAPAN PRO-WRESTLING

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:22.500
<i>Tell me, Kurachi!</i>

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.460
<i>You could have won against him!</i>

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:27.630
<i>Just tell me.</i>

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.800
<i>Why did you lose on purpose?</i>

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:32.640
<i>You said I lost on purpose?</i>

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.470
<i>You're wrong, Jun.</i>

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:37.970
<i>Pro-wrestling needs no guarding action.</i>

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.640
<i>I just absorbed all his attacks.</i>

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.690
<i>But...</i>

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:46.820
<i>this was not pro-wrestling!</i>

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:48.360
<i>Listen.</i>

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.910
<i>How could a pro-wrestler</i>
<i>not believe in pro-wrestling?</i>

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:56.870
<i>"Believe in pro wrestling."</i>

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.500
<i>Those simple words were enough for me.</i>

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.040
<i>He told me...</i>

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:06.790
<i>how a true pro-wrestler should be.</i>

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:12.680
<i>He escaped!</i>

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:17.890
<i>It's usually impossible to escape</i>
<i>from Sekibayashi.</i>

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.810
<i>This bastard...</i>

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.730
<i>When will he fall down?</i>

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.190
You don't get it?

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.820
Why do you think I don't fall down?

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:32.070
Don't chitchat while fighting.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.530
<i>But that's a part of pro-wrestling, too.</i>

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.120
You don't have a core.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:41.500
You don't love sumo, do you?

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.080
Huh?

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:46.830
I nailed it, didn't I?

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.170
Did you really show me the "true sumo"?

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:54.380
I watched it only to find it was
just an imitation of mixed martial arts.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.180
Don't make me laugh.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.850
First of all, you haven't become
a top sumo wrestler yet.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.890
So you don't deserve
to deny sumo wrestling.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:06.440
Who do you think you're talking to!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.980
Here comes an Arm Whip!

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.530
Sekibayashi has got back his momentum.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.860
Well, I think it's the right time now.

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.450
Get up, brat.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.030
You have no time left.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.120
Yeah.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.460
Right.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:29.210
Let's finish this now.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.840
<i>It's not that he's calmed down.</i>

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:35.930
<i>It's rather the opposite.</i>

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:41.890
<i>Beyond rage, this brat has</i>
<i>designs against me.</i>

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:45.140
I have had enough, trickster.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:47.940
If you don't fall,
all I need to do is to kill you.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.110
I like that, underling.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.320
Go ahead and kill me now. Huh?

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:55.360
<i>What?</i>

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:57.660
<i>Making his stance much lower?</i>

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:02.450
Pro-wrestler, you said you could absorb
all the attacks, right?

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:07.710
<i>Which part of the sumo wrestler's body</i>
<i>has the most developed muscle?</i>

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.330
<i>The answer is...</i>

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:10.750
<i>the foot!</i>

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.090
<i>He vanished?</i>
<i>No...</i>

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:17.220
<i>He's so fast that people with ordinary</i>
<i>dynamic visual acuity can't trace him.</i>

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:21.970
<i>It's a kind of headbutt</i>
<i>no one but Kiohzan can do.</i>

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:26.230
<i>It's twice as fast as normal</i>
<i>and four times as powerful as normal.</i>

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:29.480
<i>It is called Raging Vigor.</i>

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:31.650
<i>I welcome it!</i>

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.730
<i>The strongest spear...</i>

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.990
<i>and the hardest shield.</i>

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:39.320
<i>Only one of them can survive.</i>

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.490
<i>Okay, come--</i>

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:55.000
<i>That was the mightiest impact</i>
<i>that Sekibayashi had ever received.</i>

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.800
<i>Sumo overcame pro-wrestling!</i>

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:02.720
<i>However...</i>

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:07.810
<i>the price of victory was too high.</i>

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.480
<i>On the other hand...</i>

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:14.690
<i>pro-wrestlers stand up at all times!</i>

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:20.860
You see, brat?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.870
Pro-wrestlers can endure a lot, huh?

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.290
<i>How can he stand up?</i>

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.700
<i>Why am I on the ground?</i>

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.830
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI
REP. FIGHTER OF FURUMI PHARMA

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.210
Seki redirected the attack.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.210
<i>The usual receiving method is</i>
<i>to get rid of damage from yourself.</i>

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.710
<i>But Seki's method is totally opposite.</i>

00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:42.680
<i>While receiving, he disrupts his foe's</i>
<i>striking form and turns it against them.</i>

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:47.720
The stronger the foe's attack is,
the more damage the foe receives.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.560
For pro-wrestling, Seki created...

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:54.310
the super practical combat skill
to receive and inflict damage.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:56.650
Wow.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.240
<i>You understand, Cos?</i>

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.280
<i>Of course, you're an excellent fighter.</i>

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:03.820
<i>However,</i>

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:07.660
<i>it's not only because you're young that</i>
<i>you get caught off-guard when it counts.</i>

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.040
<i>What you lack is...</i>

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:11.500
<i>faith!</i>

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.630
<i>In other words, obsession!</i>

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.000
<i>A man with faith is...</i>

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.130
<i>just strong!</i>

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.090
<i>It's about 300 kg.,</i>

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:28.890
<i>a powerbomb with the weight of</i>
<i>two men directly hitting his head.</i>

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:32.810
<i>Even a sumo wrestler</i>
<i>can't avoid concussion.</i>

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.440
<i>I don't like this.</i>

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:43.610
<i>How come I lost to...</i>

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:47.030
<i>a piece of trash like him?</i>

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:50.330
Hey, boy.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:52.540
You were such a good entertainer.

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.960
Thanks to you,
I could enjoy a glorious ending.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:58.460
The game is over!

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:03.220
Seki won because
his mental preparation was better.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:07.970
The ancient sumo by Kiohzan is
a formidable technique for sure.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:11.390
But Seki's dedicated his life
to pro-wrestling

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.810
while Kiohzan gave up on sumo.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:17.810
What made Seki the winner is
his constant effort.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:21.110
It's not that sumo lost to pro-wrestling.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:25.240
Seki's backbone and pride
overwhelmed Kiohzan's technique.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.910
-Be the champion!
-Count on me!

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.950
All right, we lost!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.540
Let's accept that.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.250
Sir, is this all part of your plan?

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:44.170
Well, I'm not sure.

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:47.050
<i>We'd like to ask a favor, sir.</i>

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:49.110
<i>Kiohzan is the future leader</i>
<i>of the sumo world...</i>

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.060
KEN RYUOHZAN, SHINOBU KOUZAN
(KIOHZAN'S BROTHERS)

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:54.770
<i>...but right now, he's full of arrogance.</i>

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:58.350
<i>Please, hurt his pride.</i>

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:00.690
<i>It's for the future of sumo.</i>

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.360
<i>Moreover, for our younger brother.</i>

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.030
<i>We beg you.</i>

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:09.620
<i>Since they were kids,</i>
<i>I've looked after them.</i>

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:12.450
<i>There is no way</i>
<i>I can reject a request from them.</i>

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:16.040
<i>Now in addition to this wound</i>
<i>on my forehead,</i>

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:19.880
<i>I owe you one more thing.</i>

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.420
<i>Right, GANDAI?</i>

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.550
He got me.

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:31.640
Um... excuse me.

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:35.850
Oh, it's you.

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:39.060
I didn't expect anyone to see this.

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:41.860
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:45.570
A professional shouldn't show
how he is behind-the-scenes to anyone.

00:22:47.150 --> 00:22:49.410
Do you think I can change?

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:53.240
I'm a piece of trash.

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:56.580
I've disappointed everyone...

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.540
and I've reached rock bottom.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:04.130
Do you think a man like me
can change, too?

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:08.380
Of course, I do.

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:12.550
<i>You, too, can change for sure.</i>

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:16.220
So stop crying.

00:23:17.310 --> 00:23:18.270
Yes!

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:22.480
<i>The length of the game was</i>
<i>six minutes and 47 seconds.</i>

00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:26.070
<i>Sekibayashi proceeds to the second round.</i>

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:28.740
<i>And, Haruo Kohno has decided</i>

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:32.490
<i>to become a pupil of Jun Sekibayashi.</i>

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:07.020
PREVIEW

00:24:07.190 --> 00:24:09.490
<i>The ghost of Master Niko Tokita appears.</i>

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:12.070
<i>Cut the crap!</i>

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:15.030
<i>Ashura has no warm memories.</i>

00:24:15.240 --> 00:24:18.410
<i>How will you end up fighting when Advance</i>
<i>takes so much of your life, Ashura?</i>

00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:20.250
<i>Next episode: "Master and Pupil."</i>

00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:21.830
Subtitle translation by Hinako Someno
